  "question": {
    "text": "The densities of two solid spheres <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> of the same radii <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> vary with radial distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> as <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> , respectively, where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> is a constant. The moments of inertia of the individual spheres about axes passing through their centres are <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math> , respectively. If <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
